# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  PALA Testbed — Environment Configuration
#  IEEE S&P 2027 Artifact (Paper: Architecture-Induced Reward Hacking in
#  NWDAF-Integrated LLM Control Loops)
#
#  Step 1:  Copy this file:   cp .env.example .env
#  Step 2:  Fill in your LLM API key below (or use Ollama for local inference)
#  Step 3:  Run:              ./quickstart.sh
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  LLM BACKEND — choose ONE option
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# OPTION A — Ollama (local GPU, NO API key needed)
#   Requirements: ollama installed + model pulled (47 GB for qwen2.5:72b)
#   Install:  curl -fsSL https://ollama.ai/install.sh | sh
#   Pull:     ollama pull qwen2.5:72b
#   Note:     This is what the paper experiments used. Needs a GPU with >= 48 GB.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5:72b

# OPTION B — Google AI Studio / Gemini (cloud, no GPU needed, free tier)
#   Requirements: Free API key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#   Free tier:    15 requests/minute — sufficient for individual experiments
#   Uncomment these lines and comment out the Ollama lines above:
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your_google_ai_studio_key_here
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash

# OPTION C — OpenAI-compatible API (needs: pip install -r requirements-api.txt)
#   Supported only by wave_experiments/exp1_vuln_multimodel.py (Table 2 cross-family rows);
#   every other experiment uses Ollama. Works with Together AI, Groq, Mistral AI, and other
#   OpenAI-compatible providers.
#   For primary (Qwen 2.5 72B) via Together AI:
# OPENAI_COMPAT_KEY=your_together_key_here
# OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=https://api.together.xyz/v1
# OPENAI_COMPAT_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen2.5-72B-Instruct-Turbo
#
#   For Groq (key goes in OPENAI_COMPAT_KEY; pass the model with --api-model). Groq has
#   retired llama-3.1-70b-versatile; any model it now serves is not the paper's model.
# OPENAI_COMPAT_KEY=your_groq_key_here
# OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=https://api.groq.com/openai/v1
#
#   For Mistral Large via Mistral AI:
# OPENAI_COMPAT_KEY=your_mistral_key_here
# OPENAI_COMPAT_BASE_URL=https://api.mistral.ai/v1
# OPENAI_COMPAT_MODEL=mistral-large-latest
#
# See MODEL_SETUP.md for per-model API configuration details.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  OPEN5GS WEBUI — leave as-is for Docker testbed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker testbed maps WebUI to port 10999
WEBUI_URL=http://localhost:10999
WEBUI_USER=admin
WEBUI_PASSWORD=1423

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  MONGODB — leave as-is for Docker testbed
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Docker testbed maps MongoDB to port 27020 to avoid conflicts with native mongod
MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27020
NWDAF_DB=nwdaf_analytics

# Standard MongoDB (for non-Docker / native testbed)
# MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017

# Anthropic — E6 frontier capability tier (srsRAN track; pip install -r requirements-srsran.txt)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  srsRAN track — directory holding the srsRAN_Project/ and srsRAN_4G/ builds
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SRSRAN_BUILD=/path/to/srsran_build        # default: ~/srsran_build
